messages:
Alex K: FYI - customer hit a 422 on /v1/rerank. They embedded the query field inside each document object and we errored out. Attaching their truncated payload below.

Maria S: Can you paste the exact payload? quick repro will help.

Alex K: Here you go (sanitized):
```json
{
  "query": {
    "text": "irrelevant top-level query"
  },
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "doc-1",
      "metadata": {
        "source": "kb"
      },
      "query": "what is refund policy?",
      "text": "...doc text..."
    },
    {
      "id": "doc-2",
      "text": "...doc text..."
    }
  ]
}
```

Raj P: aha — they put a string key named "query" on each doc which shadows the top-level query. Our parser looks for top-level "query" object and rejects when nested primitive is present in docs with same key path, because we map "query" to a typed struct. error returned was: "422 Unprocessable Entity - invalid type for field 'query' in documents[0]".

Maria S: Is that a new strictness? Customer says older requests used to work.

eng-oncall: We tightened schema validation in last release to prevent ambiguous query routing (we require top-level query to be object or string and disallow the same reserved names inside doc entries unless nested under "metadata"). This was to avoid abuse where customer query is stored per-doc.

Alex K: Customer wants a workaround — they have per-document search hints stored in "query" field.

Raj P: Short-term: rename their per-doc field to "hint" or move it under "metadata.hint". Long-term: we can add a parser alias that accepts "query" under docs if present under "documents[*].attributes.query" but that's risky.

Maria S: Can we detect and auto-rename during validation with a warning instead of 422? Might be less breaking.

eng-oncall: We can add a compatibility path: if top-level "query" exists and docs have primitive "query" keys, we emit a 200 with sanitized payload and include a "warnings" array in response for one release cycle. Need an RFC.

SupportBot: Ticket #CS-10982 created. Priority: P2. Assigned: eng-oncall. ETA for hotfix RFC: 48h.

Alex K: Repro steps for eng: 1) POST to /v1/rerank 2) body as above 3) observe 422 with message "invalid type for field 'query' in documents[0]".

Raj P: Also note edge-case: if they instead used "candidates" top-level and placed per-candidate "query" strings, current schema allows "candidates[*].metadata" but still rejects reserved key "query". So docs vs candidates difference matters.

Maria S: Customer asked why passages exist in docs schema. quick explain?

eng-oncall: Passages are for when you want to send smaller context chunks; accepted shapes: top-level "passages" array OR "documents[*].passages" (each passage object must have "text"). Passages won't accept fields named "query" at top level of the passage object either.

Alex K: Customer also reported occasional all-zero scores when they tried renaming their per-doc key to "hint" and sending >100 candidates. Might be unrelated but mention here.

Raj P: That all-zeros issue is the batching limit: when candidates>100 we currently drop scoring and return zeros with no explicit error — bug logged. Separate fix.

Maria S: For now I'll reply to customer with: - immediate workaround to rename per-doc "query" to "metadata.hint" - example payload they can send - ETA for compatibility warning path 48-72h - separate follow-up for zero-scores bug.

Alex K: Example quick workaround payload I sent them:```json
{
  "query": {
    "text": "what is refund policy?"
  },
  "documents": [
    {
      "id": "doc-1",
      "metadata": {
        "hint": "what is refund policy?"
      },
      "text": "...doc text..."
    }
  ]
}
```

SupportBot: CS-10982 updated: label added: schema-compatibility.

eng-oncall: I'll draft RFC and link here. If anyone can add sample corpus where this was relied upon, paste it into the ticket.

Maria S: Thanks all, I'll update the customer thread with workarounds and the ticket link.

Alex K: Thanks — closing loop once RFC posted.
